# by-name labels are DUPLICATED across the internal eMMC (mmcblk0) and an SD card
# on the sister TAB-A03-BR, so by-name/{system,userdata,cache,...} resolve
# non-deterministically and TWRP could operate on the wrong device. Pin everything
# to the internal eMMC (mmcblk0). eMMC is mmc0 (sdhci-pxav3.2, the boot0/boot1/rpmb
# controller).
#
# VERIFIED on the BS unit (SN 0M6P034608) 2026-07-26 via
# `ls -l /dev/block/platform/soc.1/by-name/` + /proc/partitions: every p-number
# below matches. eMMC total 15388672 KB; p16 system 1941504 KB, p17 cache
# 1105920 KB, p18 userdata 12058624 KB.
#
# MMC host map on BS (NB: this corrects the note in twrp-build-tab-a03-br.md,
# which had the SD slot on mmc2):
#   mmc0 = sdhci-pxav3.2 = internal eMMC        -> mmcblk0
#   mmc1 = sdhci-pxav3.0 = external microSD slot (empty when checked)
#   mmc2 = sdhci-pxav3.1 = SDIO, WiFi (type=SDIO, mmc2:0001) -- NOT a card slot
# SDIO claims no mmcblkN, so a card in mmc1 enumerates as mmcblk1 and
# /external_sd below is right -- but this is inference, still untested with an
# actual card inserted.
/boot        emmc  /dev/block/mmcblk0p15
/recovery    emmc  /dev/block/mmcblk0p7
/system      ext4  /dev/block/mmcblk0p16
/cache       ext4  /dev/block/mmcblk0p17
/data        ext4  /dev/block/mmcblk0p18
/misc        emmc  /dev/block/mmcblk0p10
/external_sd vfat  /dev/block/mmcblk1p1 /dev/block/mmcblk1 flags=display="Micro SDcard";storage;wipeingui;removable
